{% doc %}
  The CSS custom properties that size a carousel's slides, before the module
  loads and after it.

  ## The problem this solves

  `assets/carousel.js` is a lazily loaded module, so there is always a window —
  first paint to upgrade — in which the track is laid out by the stylesheet
  alone. Without a declared slide width every slide is a flex item with the
  browser default `flex: 0 1 auto`, free to shrink: twelve announcements squeeze
  into one row and then snap to one slide when the module lands. That is the
  "it shows all 12 on page load" report, and no amount of component
  configuration fixes it, because the component is not running yet.

  The fix is to tell CSS what the slide width will be, in Liquid, in the markup.
  `carousel.css` has one generic rule that reads these properties, and it is the
  same rule before and after the module arrives — so nothing resizes on upgrade.
  A section adds no CSS of its own, now or in future.

  ## Why these are not the `--columns-*` properties the grid already uses

  `--columns-desktop` is a whole-number column count for a CSS grid. These are
  slides per view, which is a *fraction* whenever there is a peek. Same idea,
  different values, and overloading one name for both is how a 2.3-slide
  carousel ends up rendering as a 2-column grid.

  ## Parameters

  Identical to `carousel-options` so a caller passes the same arguments to both:

    settings (object, required)
    columns_mobile / columns_tablet / columns_desktop (number)
    peek_mobile / peek_desktop (number)
    space_between (number)  px. Omit to inherit the grid's own `--grid-gap-x`.
    gap_css (string)        A CSS length or `var()` for `--carousel-gap`, for a
                            caller whose spacing steps at a breakpoint and so
                            cannot be one number. Wins over `space_between`.

  ## `gap_css`, and why a number is not always enough

  `space_between` is a px value that goes into `data-options` as well, which is
  what most callers want: one number, written once.

  A carousel whose gap changes at a breakpoint cannot use it — one attribute
  cannot carry two values. Passing `gap_css` instead — `var(--something)` that a
  media query redefines — and omitting `space_between` puts the answer entirely
  in CSS, which is where the breakpoint already lives. Nothing in JavaScript
  reads the gap: `--carousel-gap` is the only spacing there is, and the slide
  width is a `calc()` built from it, so a media query that redefines the
  property moves the slides with it.

  @param {string} [gap_css]
  @param {string} [columns_desktop]
  @param {string} [columns_mobile]
  @param {string} [columns_tablet]
  @param {string} [peek_desktop]
  @param {string} [peek_mobile]
  @param {string} [space_between]


  @example
    <carousel-slider
      style="{% render 'carousel-vars', settings: section.settings %}"
      data-options="{% render 'carousel-options', settings: section.settings %}">
{% enddoc %}

{%- capture slides_mobile -%}
  {%- render 'carousel-slides',
      settings: settings,
      viewport: 'mobile',
      columns_mobile: columns_mobile,
      peek_mobile: peek_mobile,
      peek_desktop: peek_desktop -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture slides_tablet -%}
  {%- render 'carousel-slides',
      settings: settings,
      viewport: 'tablet',
      columns_tablet: columns_tablet,
      peek_mobile: peek_mobile,
      peek_desktop: peek_desktop -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture slides_desktop -%}
  {%- render 'carousel-slides',
      settings: settings,
      viewport: 'desktop',
      columns_desktop: columns_desktop,
      peek_mobile: peek_mobile,
      peek_desktop: peek_desktop -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gap = space_between | default: -1 | plus: 0

  # `-1` is the sentinel for "the caller said nothing", because `0` is a real
  # value here. Unset, the gap falls through to the grid's own spacing, so a
  # section that is a grid at one breakpoint and a carousel at another keeps one
  # rhythm across both.
  if gap_css != blank
    assign gap_value = gap_css
  elsif gap >= 0
    assign gap_value = gap | append: 'px'
  else
    assign gap_value = 'var(--grid-gap-x, 0rem)'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture vars -%}
  --carousel-slides-mobile: {{ slides_mobile | strip }};
  --carousel-slides-tablet: {{ slides_tablet | strip }};
  --carousel-slides-desktop: {{ slides_desktop | strip }};
  --carousel-gap: {{ gap_value }};
{%- endcapture -%}
{{- vars | strip_newlines | strip -}}